<title>FINLAND: MERITA SAYS EURO TO COST IT FIM 200 MLN.</title>
<headline>MERITA SAYS EURO TO COST IT FIM 200 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland largest banking group Merita Oy said in a statement on Monday that introducing Euro would cost it about 200 million markka.</p>
<p>Some 120 million of this would be in information technology.</p>
<p>&quot;The costs would be spread over the years 1997-2003,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>This year's costs of EMU preparations are less than one percent of Merita's annual costs, it said.</p>
<p>	  -- Helsinki newsroom +35 89 6805 0247</p>
</text>
